      "movement": "significant",
      "text": "Transport Minister Lulu Ranne (Finns Party) told Sisä-Suomen Lehti that Länsirata construction 'is stuck and won't proceed this government term,' triggering immediate contradiction from PM Orpo, who told reporters the project 'proceeds entirely normally' under the coalition programme and that 'nothing has been decided anywhere' about delay. Ranne subsequently clarified on X and to STT that the coalition remains committed to advancing the project, but the company operating Länsirata Oy acknowledged construction would unlikely begin before 2028. Orpo labelled Centre Party leader Kaikkonen's criticism 'politicking,' but acknowledged no government asset sales for the project are currently planned despite earlier commitments. Separately, Kauppalehti reported that NATO has placed infrastructure requirements on Finland including the Arctic rail corridor to Narvik, and that sources indicate some government politicians favour redirecting Länsirata's €385 million toward the militarily prioritised Arctic route.",
